obs Opened on an empty index and 29 stashes. The newest autostash's compiler control is byte-identical to HEAD; its record is already landed with later repair details. No stash was applied or dropped.
obs The record scan reads 27 round-open stashes, 26 records carried, zero unlanded, three orphan work files and 26 orphan account shelves. Its 107 unread paths are path-level readings, distinct from the file-version comparison below.
obs Compared 100 modified file versions under mantra, tally and tools across all 29 stashes: 42 match HEAD exactly, six patches reverse-apply cleanly, and 52 need closer review. Reverse application is evidence of patch presence, not proof that all later behavior is preserved.
obs Five older Tally roster versions differ only in whole-line comments and blank lines: cd703a04fa holds the scan and witness; 1b28f12d8a, 076ad51762 and 24efdc27b4 each hold the witness. Their executable-line comparison matches HEAD. The landed roster repair is 1be35b59d.
obs The two parked Tally caller-map drafts at 81f73d1e51 and ef3f25748f match each other but differ from the landed 349cc9d68 design. The landed guard retains its named sample beside the derived population; the existing control tests a retarget leaving that population. These drafts stay preserved for further comparison.
obs Two detached launches exited before a full verdict. Keeping the launching shell alive allowed the third pass to finish. Its actual printed transcript is session-output/standing-equipment-cold.txt; the launch head and all 16 printed stash subjects match this checkout. The first speculative shell command named an absent file and changed nothing; no result was inferred from it.
obs The full cold pass at 7d2e4d9b70 ran 208 guards: 203 green, three red including the summary, and two Pond custody gates. It held the tree still. The recovered compiler and session-roster checks pass; merge, annotation, v1, store and diff checks pass too.
obs The shell failure is a skipped proof: with rg absent, the helper reports pass=45 skip=1 fail=0 while its witness requires pass=47. Copal's card had already diagnosed the companion failure where removing rg's PATH directory also removes sh. Bakery's transcript shows seed-receipt work; Copal's shows a recovery close, with neither control edit in flight.
claim Existing shell_dialect repair on Copal's live card, taken after this seat's recovery comparison; no peer file moves and no custody gate crossed.
obs The five-tool PATH trial passes with rg absent and with rg and sh colocated. The first four-tool trial failed because xargs invokes external printf; adding that required executable lets the real scan return exit 127 and instrument=rg in both layouts.
obs The repaired helper passes 47 checks with zero skips on this host and in the colocated layout. A copied scan whose absence refusal is replaced by exit 0 fails both checks and returns control exit 1. The full shell_dialect witness passes.
obs Amphora's cold red came from an unavailable rg: its disagreement plant passed unexpectedly. The installed Nix-store rg supplied explicitly on PATH makes every Amphora bounds-agreement plant and living assertion pass; no Amphora source changed.
obs Fetched xy and fast-forwarded through 1a72d68e3f after the cold pass. Copal's recovered registrations and records remain whole. The hot pass will cover this integrated tree with the installed rg on PATH.
obs The REDS pin holds 40944 of 40960 bytes with open rows; this existing card diagnosis and the present record keep the repair visible without folding an open row or raising its bound.
